      "content": "that makes sense. but honestly, when i look at the data, it seems like the benefits for the city—like the tax revenue and the housing supply—are basically undeniable facts while the \"character\" stuff is just subjective. do you think i should just focus my presentation on the objective economic and social benefits and leave the neighborhood complaints out of the main slides? it seems like a waste of time to spend too much effort on them if they aren't based on real data.",
